    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0415" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg315"/>

                <head>No. 198.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dichman to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 20,
                        1879</date>. (Received October 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 138.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In order that the Department might be in
                    possession of the knowledge of all the successive steps taken by this government
                    in connection with the subject of the deposit of ships’ papers, I beg to inclose
                    a retranslation of that part of the report of the Colombian secretary for
                    foreign relations for 1878, which treats of this matter.</p>
                <p>The original will be forwarded by the first favorable opportunity.</p>
                <p>This report shows how the diplomatic agreement of 1876 came to be set aside, thus
                    leading to the difficulty in the case of the Lorine.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ERNEST DICHMAN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d198-a1.xml" xpointer="d198-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d198-a2.xml" xpointer="d198-a2"/>
